            <ArticleTitle>Zomepirac-induced serum sickness. A report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2812-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients, after several weeks of zomepirac sodium use, experienced acute toxic eruption, fever, lymphadenopathy, arthralgias, angioedema of the hands, and eosinophilia. We believe that these cases represent type 3 allergic reactions to zomepirac.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
